In this directory are the files necessary to compile IONe under the OpenWRT 
cross-compile framework.

The following command sequence will configure your OpenWRT environment:

First, navigate to your OpenWRT source directory.  For this example, we 
will use ~/openwrt.

echo "src-link mypackages ~/mypackages" > ~/openwrt/feeds.conf
mkdir ~/mypackages
mkdir ~/mypackages/examples
mkdir ~/mypackages/examples/IONe
cp Makefile.OpenWRT ~/mypackages/examples/IONe/Makefile
scripts/feeds update mypackages
scripts/feeds install -a -p mypackages

make menuconfig to configure your build environment, and set your target.

make -j1 V=s package/IONe/compile

If all went smoothly, you will have a binary package of IONe suitable 
for your OpenWRT installation in 
~/openwrt/bin/packages/$ARCH/mypackages/IONe/IONe-1.0.0-1_$ARCH.ipk scp 
this file from your OpenWRT device, and issue the final command, on the 
device, to install:

opkg install *ipk

